    "caption": "In 1964 a textile-mill boss shaved an eighth of a dollar off a promised buyback. Warren Buffett was so annoyed he bought the whole failing mill, which he later called his dumbest stock ever and, by his own estimate, a $200 billion mistake. The twist: the mill's name became Berkshire Hathaway.\n\nSunday special. Get this week's five, free every Saturday → link in bio.\n\n#WarrenBuffett #BerkshireHathaway #investing #stockmarket #history\n\nSources: CNBC (Oct 18 2010, Mar 2 2023), Fox Business, NPR Planet Money, AP (Sep 18 2026). Illustrated portrait. Not investment advice."
